    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d132">

                <pb facs="0269" n="170" sameAs="frus:frus1936v05/pg170"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.154/1100</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Costa
                        Rica</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Collins</hi>)<anchor n="19"
                        xml:id="d132-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 352</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-10-20">October 20, 1936</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In a letter addressed to the Secretary of
                    State on October 14, 1936,<anchor n="18" xml:id="d132-f2"/> the Acting Secretary
                    of Agriculture stated that Mr. E. W. James of the Bureau of Public Roads of that
                    Department would proceed about October 16 to Panamá, Costa Rica, Nicaragua,
                    Honduras and Guatemala, in connection with work on the Inter-American
                    Highway.</p>
                <p>Please show to Mr. James, should the occasion arise, such courtesies and render
                    to him such assistance as is possible and proper.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sumner
                            Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d132-f1" n="19" type="source" xml:id="d132-f1-content">
                <p>The same, October 20, to the American diplomatic missions in Guatemala, Honduras,
                    Nicaragua, and Panamá.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d132-f2" n="18" xml:id="d132-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
